## Workflow

```text
Reviewer sources
      ↓
Import concerns into revision-notes.md
      ↓
Group concerns by dependency into revision-ledger.md
      ↓
Author reviews and confirms the cluster sequence
      ↓
Discuss the next cluster and record the author's decisions in the notes
      ↓
Settle the selected cluster's decisions and prerequisites; authorize work
      ↓
Implement → build → inspect source diff → generate comparison
      ↓
AUTHOR-REVIEW
      ├── author approves → AUTHOR-APPROVED → next cluster discussion
      └── author reports a bounded correction → revise → AUTHOR-REVIEW
      ↓
Response materials and final global audit
      ↓
COMPLETE after explicit author approval
```

The agent first extracts concerns of referees and proposes clusters from
their dependencies. 

Follow the cluster sequence to discuss concerns and possible treatments
with the agent. It records your decisions, rationale, and intended scope
in the notes. 

The consistency check is usually used after the author do some manual
edition.

The author can report a problem in ordinary language. The agent will
preserve the report text in `revision-issues.md`, relate it to reviewer
items, and wait for correction authorization when necessary.

## Common requests

Examples of clear instructions to Codex:

- “Extract the reviewer comments and propose clusters in dependency
  order. Leave undecided items pending and do not revise the
  manuscript.”
- “I confirm this cluster sequence. Walk me through the first cluster's
  concerns and possible treatments so I can decide how to address them.”
- “Record my decision for R1-03, but do not implement it yet.”
- “I authorize implementation of Cluster 2.”
- “The comparison changes the theorem more broadly than intended. Record
  this issue and propose a bounded correction.”
- “Run a consistency check for the author-approved clusters.”
- “I approve this cluster. Advance the ledger and tell me the next
  eligible action.”

## Current status

Read `review/HANDOFF.md` for the active or most recently completed pass,
verification evidence, unresolved concerns, and the single next author
action.
